# Fleet deploy-key registry: public keys a machine accepts for exactly ONE
# command and nothing else. The sibling `fleet-keys` grants a session; a line
# here grants a forced command with no PTY, no port or agent forwarding and
# no X11 (modules/nixos/vps.nix renders each row with those options into the
# same root-owned /etc/ssh/authorized_keys.d/<user> file). Public material
# only; the private half belongs to whatever automation holds it -- for the
# manifold deploy row, a GitHub Actions repository-level credential on
# atyrode/manifold; for the plugins deploy row, the same-named credential on
# atyrode/code and atyrode/babel, whose releases hand the receiver a plugin
# bundle to install on the integrated preview -- so a workflow can trigger
# that one script on the host and cannot open a shell.
#
# A key reaches a machine only through a reviewed commit here and a redeploy;
# a line removed cannot connect. Rotate by replacing the KEY field and the
# secret on the automation side in the same hour.
#
# One line per key, whitespace-separated, four identity fields plus argv:
#
#   NAME  HOST  KEYTYPE  BASE64-KEY  COMMAND [ARG...]
#
# NAME     stable identifier, written as the comment of the rendered line.
# HOST     the fleet host id that accepts it; other hosts ignore the row.
# COMMAND  absolute executable path followed by fixed literal argument tokens.
#          No shell parsing: quotes and metacharacters are literal, not syntax;
#          whitespace cannot occur inside a token. Rendering shell-quotes every
#          token, then escapes it for the authorized_keys command option.
#          Caller text arrives only as SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND; the receiver
#          validates it within the fixed role, never as additional authority.
#          Deploy and plugin delivery deliberately use separate roles. The
#          shared own-plugin key retains Code's hardened installs and Babel's
#          in-realm installs through fixed MODE PREFIX pairs; it cannot deploy
#          revisions, change a publisher's mode or choose other publishers.

